. do "20250722_213409_01agbe_h2.do"

. **************************************************************************
. * H2: Political preferences – Analysis                      *
. * Authors: [REDACTED], [REDACTED]                                     *
. /********************************************************************
> * CHANGE LOG (July 2025):
> * Following feedback, we revised the H2 
> * analysis to ensure it yields one single testable coefficient per 
> * hypothesis. Specifically, we:
> * - Focused exclusively on the ideological self-placement variable 
> *   (`zLeftRight`) as the outcome for H2.
> * - Removed the secondary outcome based on political party affiliation 
> *   (`plh0012_h`, previously recoded into `LeftParty5`).
> *
> * This change aligns the analysis with the pre-analysis plan's DiD 
> * specification (Equation 1), and guarantees comparability across 
> * hypotheses.
> ********************************************************************/
. * clear all
. version 18

. set maxvar 10000


. 
. 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * INSTALL PACKAGES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. ssc install mdesc
checking mdesc consistency and verifying not already installed...
all files already exist and are up to date.

. 
. *-----------------------------
. * CONFIGURE FILE PATHS
. /*
> *-----------------------------
> if strpos("`c(pwd)'", "code") {
> global ROOT "`c(pwd)'/.."
> }
> else {
> global ROOT "`c(pwd)'"
> }
> global IN "$ROOT/data/raw" // folder, in which the original datasets are stor
> ed
> global DATA "$ROOT/data/derived" // folder for datasets
> global OUT "$ROOT/out" // folder for output (results, tables)
> 
> */
. 
. *============================================================================
> ===
. **# Data Preparation * 
. *============================================================================
> ===
. 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * LOAD AND MERGE DATA * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. 
. use "$IN/ppathl.dta", clear // use ppathl as a starting dataset
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

. 
. * Merge ppathl with all datasets, that you deem relevant for your analysis. (
> Tip: use keepusing() to specify which variables to keep from the using datase
> t; the default is all.)
. 
. * biobirth contains information on fertility history
. merge m:1 pid using "$IN/biobirth.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable pid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable cid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable gebjahr was int, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label sex already defined)
(label sex_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. * pgen contains user-friendly data on the individual level that are consolida
> ted from different sources
. merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. * pl contains all variables from the individual questionnaire
. merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pl.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable inputdataset was str6, now str9 to accommodate using data's values)
(label cid already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. * hgen contains generated variables on household level from the household int
> erview; use for household net income
. merge m:1 hid syear using "$IN/hgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches) keepusin
> g(hid syear hghinc)
(label iyear already defined)
(label iyear_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. 
. label language EN // change language of the labels to English

. ************************************
. save "$DATA/h2_dataset.dta", replace // save merged dataset
file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/5%-sample/h2_dataset.dta saved

. ************************************
. 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * PREPARE VARIABLES * 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. use "$DATA/h2_dataset.dta", clear

. 
. *-----------------------------
. * Construct Outcome Variables
. *-----------------------------
. 
. *–– 3.1 Clean raw items; set negatives to missing
. foreach v in plh0004 plh0012_h {
  2.     replace `v' = . if `v' < 0
  3. }
(22,543 real changes made, 22,543 to missing)
(15,982 real changes made, 15,982 to missing)

. 
. *–– 3.2 Ideological self‐placement (plh0004)
. *    Flip so higher = more left, then standardize within wave
. gen LeftRight = 10 - plh0004
(30,665 missing values generated)

. bysort syear: egen mean_LR = mean(LeftRight) if !missing(LeftRight)
(30,665 missing values generated)

. bysort syear: egen sd_LR   = sd(LeftRight)   if !missing(LeftRight)
(30,665 missing values generated)

. gen zLeftRight = (LeftRight - mean_LR) / sd_LR
(30,665 missing values generated)

. drop mean_LR sd_LR

. 
. *-----------------------------
. * 4.  Construct key regressors
. *    – Daughter_i  (firstborn=girl)
. *    – Post_i,t    (post‐birth periods)
. *-----------------------------
. * identify ever‐had a daughter/son (first child)
. bysort pid: egen byte Daughter = max(kidsex01==2)

. bysort pid: egen byte Son      = max(kidsex01==1)

. bysort pid (syear): assert Daughter==Daughter[1]    // ensure time‐invariant

. 
. * timing of birth
. gen yearFirstChild = kidgeb01

. gen byte Post = (syear >= kidgeb01) 

. 
. * gender dummy (for H4)
. gen byte Man = (sex==1)

. 
. *-----------------------------
. * 5.  Controls (Table 4 PaP) 
. *-----------------------------
. mdesc sumkids pgfamstd plh0258_h sampreg birthregion_ew bioage migback pgbilz
> eit hghinc pgemplst pgexpft

    Variable    |     Missing          Total     Percent Missing
----------------+-----------------------------------------------
        sumkids |           0         35,228           0.00
       pgfamstd |       7,823         35,228          22.21
      plh0258_h |       8,122         35,228          23.06
        sampreg |           0         35,228           0.00
   birthregio~w |           0         35,228           0.00
         bioage |           0         35,228           0.00
        migback |           0         35,228           0.00
      pgbilzeit |       7,823         35,228          22.21
         hghinc |       4,207         35,228          11.94
       pgemplst |       7,823         35,228          22.21
        pgexpft |       7,823         35,228          22.21
----------------+-----------------------------------------------

. 
. * number of children (pool 5+)
. gen nchild = sumkids

. replace nchild = 5 if nchild>5
(412 real changes made)

. 
. * marital status
. gen mastat = pgfamstd == 1 | pgfamstd == 6 | pgfamstd == 7 | pgfamstd == 8

. replace mastat = . if pgfamstd == .
(7,823 real changes made, 7,823 to missing)

. label define mastat 0 "Unmarried" 1 "Married"

. label values mastat mastat

. 
. * region of interview & origin
. replace sampreg      = sampreg - 1                   // 0=West,1=East
(35,228 real changes made)

. replace birthregion_ew = birthregion_ew - 1           // 0=West,1=East
(35,228 real changes made)

. label define ew 0 "West" 1 "East"

. label values sampreg ew

. label values birthregion_ew ew

. 
. * age & squared
. sort pid piyear

. gen age    = syear - gebjahr

. gen age_sq = age^2

. 
. * work experience & squared
. gen exp    = pgexpft
(7,823 missing values generated)

. gen exp_sq = exp^2
(7,823 missing values generated)

. 
. * employment indicator
. gen byte emplyd = inlist(pgemplst,1,2)

. label define emp 0 "Not employed" 1 "Employed"

. label values emplyd emp

. 
. * rename household income
. label variable hghinc "Household net income"

. local controls "i.nchild i.mastat i.sampreg age age_sq exp exp_sq i.migback p
> gbilzeit hghinc i.emplyd"

. global controls "`controls'"

. 
. *-----------------------------
. *   Sample restrictions (Section 4 PaP)
. *    – first‐time parents
. *    – outcome observed both before & after
. *-----------------------------
. keep if inlist(pop,1,2) // only keeping participants from private households 
> and with complete information 
(4,698 observations deleted)

. 
. * restrict to plausible ages and valid region
. keep if sampreg>=0 & inrange(age,18,50)
(14,445 observations deleted)

. 
. * must have become first‐time parent within window
. keep if yearFirstChild>0 
(4,839 observations deleted)

. 
. * Flags for zLeftRight availability pre/post
. bysort pid: egen byte has_zLR_pre  = max(!missing(zLeftRight) & !Post)

. bysort pid: egen byte has_zLR_post = max(!missing(zLeftRight) & Post)

. 
. 
. *============================================================================
> ===
. * H2 Analysis
. *============================================================================
> ===
. 
. 
. *-----------------------------
. * DiD regressions  
. *Regression : y_i,t = β_0 + β_1*Daughter_i + β_2*Post_i,t + β_3*Daughter_i × 
> Post_i,t + \gamma*X_i,t + \varepsilon_i,t
. * The study employs a difference-in-differences (DiD) design to test whether 
> having daughters leads to more left-leaning political preferences. The approa
> ch leverages the quasi-random assignment of child sex to compare individuals 
> whose first child is a girl (treatment group) versus those whose first child 
> is a boy (control group), examining changes in political attitudes before and
>  after childbirth.
. *-----------------------------
. 
. keep if has_zLR_pre & has_zLR_post
(10,222 observations deleted)

. xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2000 to 2020, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

. xtreg zLeftRight i.Daughter##i.Post i.Man $controls, vce(cluster cid)

